// REQUIRES: wasmer, wasip1-threads
// The WebAssembly end of the pipeline, threads and all: `rene build` bakes
// the runtime for `wasm32-wasip1-threads`, compiles the package through
// `rrc`, and links a wasm module through rustc; `wasmer` then runs it —
// real WASI threads sharing one linear memory, committing to one atomically
// counted, lock-guarded map (see the package's `src/lib.rr`).
//
// This is the whole cross-target story in one test: the bake, the driver's
// `--target-triple`, the polyffi textures compiled for the target, the
// launcher link, and the module actually running. It is gated on both a
// `wasmer` on PATH (or `-DREUSSIR_WASMER=`) and a rustc that ships
// `wasm32-wasip1-threads` std (`rustup target add wasm32-wasip1-threads`).
//
// The machine target lives in the manifest's `dev` profile, so there is no
// `--target` here — and no `%rrc_linker` either: this link is rust-lld's,
// not MSVC's, whatever the host is.

// RUN: %rene build --manifest-path %S/wasi_threads/rene.ncl --build-dir %t.bdir 2>%t.build.log >%t.listing
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LISTING < %t.listing

// The artifact carries the target's extension, chosen by rene from the
// triple rather than from the host.
// LISTING: {{[/\\]}}dev{{[/\\]}}threads.wasm

// Nothing on the way there disagrees about what machine this is. rustc
// spells this target `wasm32-unknown-wasi` in the bitcode it hands back for
// a polyffi texture, where LLVM's normalization of the same target name is
// `wasm32-unknown-wasip1-threads`; the gather settles that (they describe
// one machine) instead of letting the IR linker report it.
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=QUIET --allow-empty < %t.build.log

// QUIET-NOT: different target triples

// RUN: %wasmer %t.bdir/dev/threads.wasm | %FileCheck %s

// Four threads, keys 0..256 committed once each, so the fold is
// 256 * 255 / 2. A lost update or a torn count would change it — and the
// program asserts on it Rust-side before printing, so a wrong answer is a
// failure, not a smaller number. This is also what makes the run a real
// test of the implied `+atomics`: the reference counts here are contended.
// CHECK: parallel shared map: 32640

// A second build is up to date: the wasm bake and the products are
// recorded under the target, like any other.
// RUN: %rene -v build --manifest-path %S/wasi_threads/rene.ncl --build-dir %t.bdir 2>%t.fresh.log >%t.fresh.listing
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FRESH < %t.fresh.log

// FRESH: up to date
